\ GBA notes
\ 32-bit ARM v7 TDMI, 16.78MHz (roughly 60ns each) (Thumb support)
\ Little-endian

\ Not targeting an interactive system on the GBA; rather this is using the
\ metacompiler to target the GBA with a game.

\ See gba/DESIGN.md for most of the details!

\ Initial setup for TC-Forth on Gameboy Advance.
: tc-machine S" gba" ;

REQUIRE ../host/vocabularies.ft
REQUIRE ../host/helpers.ft

host definitions

\ Metacompiler configuration =================================================
host REQUIRE ../host/configuration.ft

rom-application! \ No dictionary (+ names indirected); data indirect.
\ Then borrowing the ARM configuration of cell widths etc.
host REQUIRE ../arm/config.ft
headless!

\ TODO: Probably support multitasking in GBA? But for now it's extra setup
\ complexity we can avoid.
false TO multitasking?
false TO keyboard-input?
false TO keyboard-output?

?stack-clear

\ Target spaces ==============================================================
REQUIRE ../host/spaces.ft
split-spaces!

\ For the GBA, the name space is not present on the target.
\ The data space is separate and starts empty, because it's in a separate RAM.
REQUIRE header.ft

?stack-clear
\ The header goes at the start of the file and the start of ROM at $08000000.
\ It's 192 bytes long, so the code section can start right after it.

\ The 256B at the top of IWRAM ($03007f00 to $03007fff) are reserved for the
\ interrupt vector, interrupt stack and BIOS call stack.
\ There's 32KB of IWRAM, and I want a handful of tasks to fit into it.
\ Reserving 2KB for the interrupt bits, global VARIABLEs and miscellany, that
\ leaves 30KB for tasks. 30KB would give:
\ - 40 tasks 192 cells
\ - 32 tasks 240 cells
\ - 16 tasks 480 cells

\ We'll allow for variable-sized tasks in any case.

\ Make the generic Forth data space be the fast one and track how big it gets.
?stack-clear
\ EWRAM
$40000 allocate throw THERE-PTR CONSTANT ewram \ 256KiB
$02000000 ewram ORG!                           \ Memory map
ewram blank-space!                             \ Not in the ROM.

\ IWRAM
$8000  allocate throw THERE-PTR CONSTANT iwram \ 32KiB
$03000000 iwram ORG!                           \ Memory map
iwram blank-space!                             \ Not in the ROM.

\ Use IWRAM as the default Forth data space.
iwram TO data-space

data-space copied! \ TODO: Remove this! But for now it's needed for CONSTANTs
\ and VALUEs to work properly.
